\printbibliography

\appendix

\chapter{Rules for Counterpoint}

\section{Basic rules}
\label{app:basic_rules}

Rules used to generate the counterpoint example in
Figure~\ref{ly:basic_counterpoint}:

\begin{itemize}
	\item only whole notes
	\item end on tonic
	\item opening interval
	\item only consonances
	\item only diatonic pitches
	\item no parallel perfect intervals
	\item penultimate pitch
\end{itemize}

\section{Common rules}
\label{app:common_rules}

\begin{itemize}
	\item no voice crossing
	\item no interior unisons
	\item no repeated pitches
	\item no similar motion to perfect interval
	\item no ascending leaps larger than a minor sixth
	\item no descending leaps larger than a perfect fifth
\end{itemize}

\section{Guidelines}
\label{app:guidelines}

\begin{itemize}
	\item the melodic range should not exceed 16 semitones
	\item no more than 3 consecutive intervals
	\item no more than 3 consecutive thirds
	\item no more than 3 consecutive sixths
	\item the voices should never be more than a twelfth apart
	\item leading tone must resolve upward
	\item no more than 2 consecutive leaps in the same direction
	\item
		large leaps (larger than a third) must be balanced by a step in the
		opposite direction
\end{itemize}

